<title>DENMARK: Oresund Consortium sets 4 pct bond price at 90.35.</title>
<headline>Oresund Consortium sets 4 pct bond price at 90.35.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Danish-Swedish Oresund Consortium's four percent, 300 million Danish crown 2002 bond announced last week will be issued at 90.35, with an effective yield of 5.95 percent, lead manager Carnegie Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue price is being set to equal the effective yield to the investor of the Danish government six percent 2002 bond plus 0.05 percent, in accordance with the conditions of the published prospectus,&quot; a Carnegie statement said.</p>
<p>--Uffe Hansen, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969658</p>
